      {
        "id": "s28_note",
        "type": "flograph.util.note",
        "pos": [
          0,
          -540
        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "## Three ways to draw one slicer\n\nThe **Slicer** takes more than one column. Name two \u2014 `region, store` \u2014 and\nit becomes a **tree**: tick a region for the whole region, tick one store to\nnarrow to it, and a region with only some of its stores ticked draws a\npart-filled box.\n\n**Layout** then decides how that selection is *drawn*, and nothing else:\n\n- **list** \u2014 the checkbox list, a tree when there is more than one column\n- **cards** \u2014 a tile per value, wrapping to the width of the card\n- **dropdown** \u2014 the whole picker behind one button saying what is picked\n\nThe three slicers below are chained, so they read as one filter panel: each\none filters what the next one offers. Open the **Filter Panel** page to see\nthem as a dashboard. Layout, **Show row counts** and the card's size are all\ncosmetic \u2014 changing them never re-runs the flow.",
          "width": 560,
          "height": 260
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null
      }
